  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-browser",
      "text": "Drive the local Chrome/Edge from DeepSeek Harness (real browser, local-only)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "- `browser_open` - open a URL (lazy-launches the browser, reuses it)\n- `browser_snapshot` - title / url / interactive selectors / console errors / visible text\n- `browser_click` - click by CSS selector\n- `browser_type` - fill inputs (optional Enter)\n- `browser_press` - keyboard keys\n- `browser_scroll` - scroll or bring element into view\n- `browser_evaluate` - run JS in the page\n- `browser_screenshot` - save PNG (feed to vision tools)\n- `browser_wait` - wait ms\n- `browser_close` - close the instance"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "One lazy browser instance (headful by default so you see what the agent does),\nlaunched via `playwright-core` against the system Chrome/Edge; no browser\ndownload, no external daemon, nothing leaves the machine."
    }
  ],
